KG42.register("clusters-9c521f1c3ba60cf3e29645f0",{"id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v142-d-K002","paper":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","label":"Price-taker response, billing, and competitive-equilibrium welfare benchmark","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Price-taker response, billing, and competitive-equilibrium welfare benchmark","market_meaning":"Given a price vector, the user chooses consumption based on the benefit obtained after deducting usage-based payment from utility, and bears the corresponding time-period charges. The source also gives a benchmark in which a welfare-optimal competitive equilibrium exists under conditions, but the scope of application among general given prices, marginal-cost prices, and the welfare conclusions of the frozen chains remains to be clarified.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"All three chains belong to the price-taker case, and the billing term and the best response use the same given price. The welfare conclusion of R004 involves marginal-cost pricing and equilibrium existence and cannot be directly inferred from individual optimality under an arbitrary fixed price; its quantifiers and price-formation conditions have not yet been clarified.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Usage-based billing constitutes the payment term in the user's benefit; the best response defines the user-side condition of the competitive equilibrium; and the welfare chain provides the social-objective benchmark for that equilibrium. The best-response formulations of R005 and R004 are retained as alternative presentations and are not counted as separate independent rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides competitive-equilibrium conditions and a welfare result whose quantifiers and pricing conditions remain to be specified."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"alternative","rationale":"Retains another frozen formulation of the same price-taker best-response condition and presents it in association with R004-C002."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the obligation that consumption quantity and the given time-period price determine the user's charges."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-N01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-lambda-k"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-T001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E23"],"rationale":"The accumulated time-period charges constitute the payment term in the user's benefit, and the user maximizes this net benefit under the same fixed price vector. This connection does not prescribe how the provider forms prices."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-N02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007"],"rationale":"Both chains express equilibrium best response under a given price; R004 explicitly expands the benefit definition, and R005 references that definition. Their formulations and local roles are retained, and no additional equilibrium rule is added on this basis."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e007"],"rationale":"Both places use the price-coordination node for the price-taker case; the normalization for presentation does not add a price-generation formula."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-xn","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007"],"rationale":"Both are the consumption vector of the same user in the price-taker best-response condition, retaining the respective local roles of clearing and coordination."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-lambda-k","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-lambda-k"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007"],"rationale":"Under the same price-vector instance and time period, the two are the price components used for benefit calculation and billing. The given-price input role and the equilibrium-price role are retained, and no arbitrary given price is deemed to be a welfare-optimal price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O04","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007"],"rationale":"The two share the best-response condition; R004 additionally explicitly expands the benefit function, while R005 retains a reference to its definition. Together with their respective roles and condition associations, they are presented without selecting a unique formulation."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"scope_conflict","description":"Proposition 1 explicitly states that there exists an allocation-optimal competitive equilibrium; the summary in R004-C001 does not distinguish this existence result from the welfare optimality of all equilibria. Best response under an arbitrary given price is also insufficient to supply that conclusion.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-lambda-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream and manual work are to clarify the quantifiers, equilibrium scope and price-taking conditions of the welfare result; retain the existing assertion in frozen C and display this difference."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R004 lacks definitions of the complete welfare objective, costs and feasible set within the scope of M02, and also lacks the formation formula for marginal-cost prices; R005 and R006 only provide individual response and billing and cannot supply the provider-side pricing and welfare closure conditions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-lambda-k","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-X001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Implement the existing C2 revision request for R004 and supplement the objective, feasible region, cost conditions and marginal-cost pricing sources applicable to M02; parts for which no formula is provided remain explicitly blank and are not filled by borrowing M01 or M03 objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The generic price-coordination and welfare nodes do not yet fully express the price-taker competitive equilibrium and its existence, and the related proposals remain in pending status.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E23"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-P01"],"required_work":"Manually check the competitive-equilibrium node proposals and the welfare-optimal scope in their definitions, and then decide whether to extend the framework."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"All citations in this cluster remain unaudited candidate evidence; in particular, the equilibrium definition, proposition quantifiers and marginal-cost pricing account have not yet been checked against independent sources.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the above sources and the mappings in this cluster; experimental candidate status does not change the unverified status and does not constitute scientific acceptance."}]},"rule_refs":["36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R004","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R005","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R006"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","COMP-5d140b5f1b233ac4","COMP-6ba786383d08116d"]});
